    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. There's a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes \u2014 including the new `bulkSignupWarning` assertion.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the bulk-signup warning so that `POST /api/owners` records, and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns, a `bulkSignupWarning` flag that is `true` when more than 80 owners had already been created for that owner's registration date at creation time, else `false`.\n\nFollowing the existing pattern for creation-time snapshot fields (`namesakeCount`, `customerCode`, `householdId`), the value is computed at create time and persisted:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` and its mapstruct mapping pick it up automatically).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` (`Boolean`) column, getter, and setter.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 reused the daily-registration accumulation path: factored the per-day count into a shared `countRegisteredOn(registrationDate)` helper (also feeding the existing daily-limit reject), and set `bulkSignupWarning = registeredThatDay > 80`. Added a named `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant alongside the existing limit constants.\n- **Schema files** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column.\n\nThe threshold is \"more than 80 **already** created,\" so it counts owners persisted *before* the current create (matching the daily-limit rule's semantics): the flag first turns `true` on the 82nd create of the day.\n\nVerified: `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
